@startuml
title Two customers compete for the last 20g
participant "Request A" as A
database "PostgreSQL\nIngredient stock=20g" as DB
participant "Request B" as B
A -> DB: BEGIN; SELECT ... FOR UPDATE
DB --> A: Lock acquired, stock=20g
B -> DB: BEGIN; SELECT ... FOR UPDATE
note right of B: Wait for A's lock
A -> DB: Validate demand=20g; subtract 20g
A -> DB: Write Order A and reservation snapshot
A -> DB: COMMIT, release row lock
DB --> B: Lock acquired; current stock=0g
B -> B: demand=20g > stock=0g
B -> DB: ROLLBACK
B --> B: Reject order, no snapshot or deduction
note over A, B: Locks exist only during short DB transactions, not while browsing or paying.
@enduml
